 "note": "RPCS3 Core 931 = Core 930 plus the thermal chantier (maintainer, 11 Nov 2026; docs/rpcs3-core931-chantier-thermique.md): the hot-path counters of the SPU PUTLLC writer lock and of the PPU parks keep one cache line per thread and the lock's phases are published after its release (REWINDBOX_HOT_COUNTERS_931, REWINDBOX_WRITER_RECORD_AFTER_RELEASE_931; same values, same report); from the serious thermal state the writer park spin, the PPU passive-lock spin and the idle RSX FIFO wait on the watched word with the ARM exclusive monitor, same condition and same bound (REWINDBOX_THERMAL_POLICY_931, setting Event Waits When Hot, Automatic by default); COREPROF ENERGY931 and THERMAL931 report the energy per frame, the performance-core share, timer wakeups and the thermal state (REWINDBOX_ENERGY_931); the emulation pauses in the background and resumes only a pause it made (REWINDBOX_BACKGROUND_PAUSE_931). Core 930 unchanged otherwise. Replaces the Core 930 pin directly (Core 929 kept as the fallback in docs/evidence/rpcs3-core929). No codegen input changes: PPU and SPU codegen identities unchanged. MoltenVK dependency of run 42998604606 (libMoltenVK.a d19d3a42). Request 1 (fa363abf, run 43030700177) stopped at the iOS syntax gate: mach/mach_time.h was missing for mach_timebase_info in the ENERGY931 code; its Apple host harness job was green, the thermal harness running the LDAXR/WFE path on Apple ARM64. Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 43038892948, attempt 1, source 41427927; Apple host harnesses run 43038892948 on 41427927). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle); the packaged library holds the ENERGY931 and THERMAL931 lines, the setting and the pause queue. Not measured on the iPhone; no energy, temperature or FPS claim.",
